{"content":[{"c":["GALEED"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name meaning literally “a heap of witness.” Jacob gave this name to a pile of stones erected as a witness to the pact of friendship made between himself and his father-in-law, Laban, who named the cairn Jegar-sahadutha (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.31.47-48","r":"Gen.31.47-48","rawR":"Gen.31.47-48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.31.47-48","value":"Gen.31.47-48"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 31:47-48"},"). Its location is unknown. The name Galeed is not to be confused with the name Gilead, designation of the territory east of the Jordan."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Galeed","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 31:47-48","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.31.47-48","rawQueryValue":"Gen.31.47-48","sourceRefExact":"Gen.31.47-48"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1bcdc6ad839f373d4c75edf5ffb77fcf48bed33d5b4e53bfdec9170463e02893","sourceItemName":"Galeed","sourceItemOrder":27,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Galeed","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Galeed","title":"Galeed","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}